&lt;p&gt;Brand tracking tools help growth marketers gauge what people say about the brand, whether it’s good or bad, and why they choose competitors, all at scale. Brand monitoring also reveals AI share of voice and what you should improve to be cited more by LLMs.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;However, as with everything in marketing, brand tracking software isn’t a single tool. Brand trackers vary by metrics, AI tracking features, a company’s growth stage, use cases, and pricing.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This post breaks down the differences between brand tracking and brand monitoring, how to choose the best brand tracking tools, like HubSpot AEO, and how to confidently run a brand tracking survey. Let’s dive into the details so you can confidently choose the best-fit brand tracker.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-are-brand-tracking-tools"&gt;What are brand tracking tools?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#brand-tracking-tools-vs-brand-monitoring"&gt;Brand Tracking Tools vs. Brand Monitoring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#which-brand-tracking-metrics-matter"&gt;Which brand tracking metrics matter?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#ai-brand-tracking-and-predictive-alerts"&gt;AI Brand Tracking and Predictive Alerts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-choose-brand-tracking-tools"&gt;How to Choose Brand Tracking Tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#best-brand-tracking-tools-by-growth-stage"&gt;Best Brand Tracking Tools by Growth Stage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-run-a-brand-tracking-survey"&gt;How to Run a Brand Tracking Survey&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-brand-tracking-tools"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Brand Tracking Tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are brand tracking tools?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A brand tracking tool is software that measures &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/website/brand-health"&gt;brand health&lt;/a&gt; across channels over time. Modern brand tracking tools collect data from social platforms, search signals, PR coverage, web analytics, customer feedback, answer engines, and brand tracking surveys.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In 2026, the biggest shift is AI visibility. For brand teams, this changes the old workflow. A brand tracker no longer sits only inside quarterly brand perception research. It now integrates survey data, social listening, search demand, AI citations, customer feedback, and CRM reporting into a single decision-making dashboard.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For AI brand tracking, growth teams use &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; to monitor how a brand appears across ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini, including AI visibility scores, competitor comparisons, prompt tracking, and citation analysis. With HubSpot AEO, teams clearly understand which sources and content types AI engines cite most.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But before measurement begins, the brand foundation &lt;em&gt;must&lt;/em&gt; be clear. Use &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/create-brand-style-guide"&gt;HubSpot’s Free Brand Building Guide&lt;/a&gt; to document positioning, voice, and visual identity before measuring whether the market understands them.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Brand Tracking Tools vs. Brand Monitoring&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand tracking&lt;/strong&gt; measures longitudinal changes in &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/brand-awareness"&gt;brand awareness&lt;/a&gt;, perception, consideration, preference, and loyalty.&lt;strong&gt; Brand monitoring&lt;/strong&gt; focuses on live detection of brand mentions across the web, social channels, media, forums, reviews, and answer engines. Each solves a different problem:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand tracking answers what’s going on overall. &lt;/strong&gt;Are target buyers more aware of us this quarter? Do they prefer us over competitors? Are campaigns shifting perception?&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand monitoring answers what’s going on today.&lt;/strong&gt; Who mentioned us today? Did sentiment spike? Which creator, journalist, customer, or AI answer changed the conversation?&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Continuous listening captures ongoing brand mentions and sentiment shifts between survey waves. A brand tracking survey adds structured feedback that listening tools cannot capture on their own.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Scaling companies, oftentimes, need both to run in parallel. Brand monitoring spots a signal such as a spike in Reddit mentions, for example. Brand tracking proves whether the signal changes market perception. AI brand tracking shows whether answer engines started repeating that narrative when buyers ask for vendor recommendations.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Here is a clear distinction between brand tracking and brand monitoring for decision-makers&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Which brand tracking metrics matter?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The right brand tracking metrics show how visible, trusted, preferred, and commercially useful a brand has become. These are the core metrics worth tracking first.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ol start="1"&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand awareness&lt;/strong&gt; measures whether the market knows the brand exists.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consideration&lt;/strong&gt; measures whether buyers would include the brand in their shortlist. A crucial metric since awareness without consideration creates expensive reach and weak demand.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share of voice&lt;/strong&gt; gauges how visible the brand is compared with competitors across media, social, search, PR, and other defined channels.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentiment&lt;/strong&gt; analyzes whether brand mentions are positive, neutral, or negative.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand preference&lt;/strong&gt; measures whether buyers choose the brand over alternatives.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share of search&lt;/strong&gt; measures branded search demand against competitors.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI share of voice&lt;/strong&gt; tracks how often a brand is mentioned in AI-generated answers compared with competitors across tracked prompts and topics.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPS&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;Net Promoter Score)&lt;/strong&gt; measures customers’ willingness to recommend the brand.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CSAT (Customer Satisfaction Score) &lt;/strong&gt;gauges satisfaction following a specific interaction with a brand, product, or service.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline influence&lt;/strong&gt; measures whether brand visibility correlates with business outcomes, including branded search, direct traffic, demo requests, MQLs, SQLs, win rate, deal velocity, and retention.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ol&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Brand strength rarely fails in one place, so all these metrics matter. For example, share of voice can grow because of negative coverage — and marketers definitely want to know this.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot...

&lt;p&gt;If you’re comparing &lt;strong&gt;Scrunch versus Peec AI&lt;/strong&gt;, you need to know your buyers are already forming opinions about your brand in answer engines like ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google AI Mode before they ever reach your website.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Furthermore, if you don’t know how your brand appears in those answers, or if it appears at all, you won’t be able to best optimize your content for a channel that is increasingly shaping first impressions.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://scrunch.com/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scrunch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px;"&gt;and&lt;a href="https://peec.ai/?"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Peec&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://peec.ai/?"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are two of the most-evaluated AEO platforms for solving the challenge of AEO optimization. Both track brand visibility across &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/how-qwen-2.5-just-beat-top-ai-models"&gt;AI engines&lt;/a&gt;. But they’re built around different assumptions about what your team actually needs.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;To help you determine which AEO platform is best for you and your team, this guide compares the features, methodology, exports, use cases, and risks of Scrunch Peec AI.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-peec-ai-what-should-your-team-choose"&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: What should your team choose?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-peec-ai-features-and-pricing"&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: Features and Pricing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-peec-ai-tracking-and-accuracy"&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: Tracking and Accuracy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-peec-ai-exports-and-seats"&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: Exports and Seats&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-peec-ai-use-cases-and-fit"&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: Use Cases and Fit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-peec-ai-risks-and-caveats"&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: Risks and Caveats&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#aeo-checklist-for-scrunch-vs-peec-ai-buyers"&gt;AEO Checklist for Scrunch vs. Peec AI Buyers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#from-insights-to-outcomes-with-hubspot"&gt;From Insights to Outcomes With HubSpot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-scrunch-vs-peec-ai"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Scrunch vs. Peec AI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: What should your team choose?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The right tool fits how your team works, from your reporting cadence to your technical maturity, and what you need to do with the data once you have it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Scrunch fits your existing stack investment if you are a CMO or VP of Marketing who needs AI visibility as part of a board-level narrative and wants that visibility tied to a DXP like Sitecore or a CMS workflow. However, if you want a clean, standalone tracking and stakeholder reporting without enterprise procurement, Peec AI is the faster option.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If you are an SEO lead or content strategist who needs daily prompt-level tracking, engine coverage across the most-used answer engines, and a reporting layer you can bring to clients or internal stakeholders without design work, Peec AI is the more purpose-built choice.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scrunch’s&lt;/strong&gt; brand narrative and descriptor analysis is the best solution &lt;strong&gt;if you are a PR or brand manager&lt;/strong&gt; tracking how AI engines characterize your brand.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a RevOps or marketing ops lead&lt;/strong&gt; who needs clean data exports, Looker Studio connectors, or API/MCP integrations for attribution reporting, &lt;strong&gt;Peec AI’s&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced plan and &lt;strong&gt;Scrunch’s&lt;/strong&gt; native Looker integration both serve this workflow.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If your team is new to AEO&lt;/strong&gt; and is still validating whether AI visibility tracking belongs in the budget, &lt;strong&gt;Peec AI’s&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://peec.ai/pricing"&gt;Starter tier&lt;/a&gt; ($95/month, unlimited users, daily tracking) is the lower-risk entry point.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If your team is mature in AEO and runs on Sitecore or is evaluating a DXP&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Scrunch&lt;/strong&gt; increasingly makes sense as the combined platform deepens. Still, teams should evaluate the integration roadmap before assuming feature parity with the standalone product.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro tip:&lt;/strong&gt; The most common evaluation mistake teams make is choosing a tool based on engine count. What matters more is whether the tool measures those engines in a methodologically consistent way and whether the output maps to your reporting needs. A tool that covers six engines with API-based sampling and one that covers three engines with front-end monitoring will give you very different data.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Scrunch vs. Peec AI: Features and Pricing&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Side-by-side Feature Comparison&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pricing at a Glance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scrunch:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Core: $250/month — 125 custom prompts, 5 users&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Enterprise: Custom&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peec AI:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Starter: $95/month — 50 prompts, choose 3 models, unlimited users, daily tracking&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Pro: $245/month — 150 prompts, 2 projects&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Advanced: $495/month — 350 prompts, 5 projects, Looker Studio integration&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Enterprise: Custom — all models, API, MCP, SSO&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we like:&lt;/strong&gt; Peec AI’s unlimited-user model across all tiers is unusual in this category. Most AEO platforms charge per seat, which makes team cost hard to predict as you add stakeholders. Scrunch’s per-user fee structure on lower tiers adds up quickly for teams with more than three or four collaborators.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Differences Worth Flagging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Branded versus non-branded prompts:&lt;/strong&gt; Scrunch’s default prompt library skews toward brand-name queries. Peec AI lets you build a custom prompt library from scratch, which is important for teams tracking non-branded category prompts where your brand might appear without being named — a common AEO misstep.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sitewide versus page analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Scrunch analyzes individual pages. For teams that want to understand how the full content architecture influences AI citation patterns, this creates gaps that sitewide tools like Profound address more completely.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update cadence:&lt;/strong&gt; Peec AI’s daily tracking matters for teams in competitive or fast-mo...

&lt;p&gt;In today’s digital world, customers want to access support quickly via their preferred communication channel. In response, more companies are looking to deliver seamless, personalized support experiences via omnichannel customer service models.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=da4cd5ec-3389-4882-b6e9-e8d6ff989255&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Click Here to Get HubSpot's Customer Service Software" height="59" width="497" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/da4cd5ec-3389-4882-b6e9-e8d6ff989255.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Omnichannel customer service offers flexibility and personalization, which can improve everything from &lt;a href="https://www.plivo.com/blog/omnichannel-customer-service-statistics-you-should-know/%23:~:text%3DCompanies%2520utilizing%2520an%2520integrated%2520omnichannel%2520solution%2520experience%2520a%252031%2525%2520reduction%2520in%2520first%252Dresolution%2520times%2520and%2520a%252039%2525%2520decrease%2520in%2520customer%2520wait%2520times%2520compared%2520to%2520those%2520operating%2520in%2520silos.%2520(Zendesk)"&gt;resolution times&lt;/a&gt; to overall &lt;a href="https://www.salesmate.io/blog/customer-service-statistics/%23:~:text%3DOmnichannel%2520service%2520lifts%2520CSAT%2520to%252067%2525%252C%2520compared%2520to%2520just%252028%2525%2520for%2520disconnected%2520multichannel%2520setups."&gt;customer satisfaction&lt;/a&gt; rates. In this guide, we’ll explore omnichannel customer service and its benefits, as well as break down how to build an omnichannel service strategy and tips for buying the right omnichannel platform.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-is-omnichannel-customer-service"&gt;What is omnichannel customer service?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#omnichannel-customer-service-vs-multichannel-support"&gt;Omnichannel Customer Service vs. Multichannel Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#benefits-of-omnichannel-customer-service"&gt;Benefits of Omnichannel Customer Service&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#omnichannel-customer-service-platform-features"&gt;Omnichannel Customer Service Platform Features&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#omnichannel-customer-service-strategy"&gt;Omnichannel Customer Service Strategy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#omnichannel-customer-service-metrics-and-governance"&gt;Omnichannel Customer Service Metrics and Governance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-choose-an-omnichannel-customer-service-platform"&gt;How to Choose an Omnichannel Customer Service Platform&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-omnichannel-customer-service"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Omnichannel Customer Service&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is omnichannel customer service?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Omnichannel customer service is a service strategy designed to create a connected, consistent experience for customers across every communication channel, whether it’s email, live chat, phone, &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/service/social-media-customer-service"&gt;social media&lt;/a&gt;, or &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/service/customer-self-service"&gt;self-service&lt;/a&gt; experiences.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An omnichannel service model ensures that customer history, context, and key data are connected across channels. This approach gives support teams the full context they need to provide faster, more personalized service. Omnichannel service enhances the customer experience by removing the need for customers to repeat themselves and offering the flexibility of starting a conversation on one channel and continuing it on another.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Omnichannel Customer Service vs. Multichannel Support&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;While these terms are often used interchangeably, &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/service/omnichannel-customer-service"&gt;omnichannel customer service&lt;/a&gt; differs from multichannel support.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multichannel customer service&lt;/strong&gt; means a business simply offers support through multiple channels, but those channels may operate independently with their own inbox or ticketing queue. Multichannel service offers the convenience of multiple channels for support, but customers often need to repeat information and agents don’t have full conversation history and context when a customer switches channels.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Omnichannel customer service&lt;/strong&gt; builds upon multichannel support by connecting those channels into a single, unified experience. In omnichannel service, customer conversations, purchase history, previous interactions, and other key context are shared across channels so that agents have a unified view of customer data and customers can continue their conversation without having to start over.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Most modern omnichannel customer service platforms consolidate support requests from each channel into a shared inbox or ticketing queue, giving agents a complete view of each customer’s history to help them continue conversations seamlessly.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits of Omnichannel Customer Service&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;CX leaders who implement omnichannel customer service see tangible benefits for both their customers and their support teams. Here is a list of five key benefits of omnichannel customer service in more detail.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Reduces friction for customers.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;According to research from &lt;a href="https://event.hbrturkiye.com/storage/uploads/state-of-the-connected-customer-655b114557dfa.pdf"&gt;Salesforce&lt;/a&gt;, 56% of customers have to re-explain their issue every time they’re transferred to a different person or department. Omnichannel customer service eliminates this friction point by preserving conversation history and customer context across every touchpoint, which &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/service/reduce-customer-effort-tips"&gt;reduces friction&lt;/a&gt; for the customer when they reach out for support. When context is carried across channels, customers can pick up where they left off and aren’t required to repeat themselves, resulting in a smoother support experience.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Enables faster, more efficient support.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When customer context, history, and account information are centralized in an omnichannel customer service platform, agents spend less time looking for previous interaction history and can instead jump right in to helping solve the customer’s problem.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;With tools like HubSpot’s &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/crm/ai-crm"&gt;Smart CRM&lt;/a&gt;, agents have access to a unified customer record that is automatically enriched with data from emails, calls, and the web, giving them full context before every interaction.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A unified conversation timeline reduces context switching and information gathering for service agents. Agents can also better prioritize urgent issues and resolve requests more efficiently, which allows them to handle a larger volume of requests without compromising the quality of support.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Creates more personalized customer experiences.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://hyken.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/ACA-STATE-OF-CX-2026.pdf"&gt;Research&lt;/a&gt; shows that up to 82% of customers prefer companie...

&lt;p&gt;CRM projects don’t fail at the technical level — they fail because the people expected to use the system never bought in, the training was too generic to stick, and nobody owned adoption after go-live. The result is a CRM that costs money to maintain but doesn’t deliver the pipeline visibility or process alignment it was supposed to.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=b173b371-487a-4b24-8d8d-508e4cff3779&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Learn more about why HubSpot's CRM platform has all the tools you need to grow  better." height="58" width="802" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/b173b371-487a-4b24-8d8d-508e4cff3779.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Getting change management CRM implementation right means addressing the people and process challenges before, during, and after launch, not just configuring the software.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide covers the CRM change management strategy, team structure, communication plan, and adoption metrics that turn a CRM deployment into a system teams actually use.&lt;/p&gt; 
