&lt;p&gt;SEO might feel like it’s under threat with the rise of AI. But the data tells a different story — SEO tools are still a must-have for marketers. In a &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/marketing-statistics"&gt;HubSpot survey&lt;/a&gt;, 27% of marketers agreed that the biggest ROI channel of this year was the website, blog, and SEO.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=1c4e7d6c-5c7e-4ae1-b7c5-0c524b4c0210&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Learn More About HubSpot's SEO &amp;amp; Content Strategy Tool" height="59" width="520" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/1c4e7d6c-5c7e-4ae1-b7c5-0c524b4c0210.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;It’s fair to say that SEO has changed, but it’s still an essential component of a successful marketing strategy. The key is having an excellent strategy, timely execution, and stakeholder buy-in, with reporting that proves the channel’s success. All of this hinges on picking the best SEO marketing software. It ‌means choosing a stack that drives the business forward without breaking the bank.&lt;/p&gt; 
